prepare_plan.py --candidate NN [--cli-candidate 09] creates a fresh planned-NN
folder containing two specs for the unchanged runtime-coverage/reconcile.py and
an explicit audit-plan.json. These are only planned paths; absent required
receipts cannot be skipped. The generator refuses existing plan directories.

Before execution, root/reviewer must align the plan's focused runs and supporting
inputs with actual named final receipts and source reviews. Create a new plan
filename rather than altering any spec that has already generated a proof.
All ordinary, inventory and sanitizer paths must refer to the final snapshot.
Only release/CLI may reuse an earlier snapshot, and only after the checker proves
all production, package, script, fixture and resource bytes are identical. A passing09 production
build cannot replace final ordinary/sanitizer evidence.

audit-final.py --config planned-NN/audit-plan.json --output review-NN-source.json
requires completed exact-source runs, both reconciliation proofs, raw captures,
XML, exact parameter argument-start multisets and aggregate completions. It uses
its own second parser, independently of reconcile.py. It refuses output overwrite.
No skipped declarations or known-issue completions are treated as passed.
The original audit.py remains byte-preserved because preparation-10.json records
it; audit-final.py additionally verifies discovery-helper and planned-command identity.

These tools cannot certify external conformance or peers, Linux execution, OS26
runtime, full-cross-target concurrent sanitizer execution, or whole-R3 acceptance.
The CLI/process report verifies local assertions and expected exit codes only.
